    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50232" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vā^sātes</span></b> , um,
		and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vā^sātae</span></b> ,
			ārum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Aquitania</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Parent. 24</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 11,
			14</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vā^sātĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Vasates</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rheda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 7, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
